        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Firefox 141 supports <code class=\"notranslate\">webkitdirectory</code> on android in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1887878\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1887878</a>, which was added in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3161889553\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27108\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27108/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27108\">#27108</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">What this does is allow you to mark that an input offers a folder selector, and when you select a folder it returns an array of <code class=\"notranslate\">File</code> entries with the path in the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/File/webkitRelativePath\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">File.webkitRelativePath</code></a> property (see <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLInputElement/webkitdirectory#examples\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">HTMLInputElement.webkitdirectory</code></a> for detail).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">But it turns out that on Firefox for Android the returned <code class=\"notranslate\">webkitRelativePath</code> is always an empty string.<br>\nWhat I think this means is that FF supports <code class=\"notranslate\">webkitRelativePath</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">HTMLInputElement/webkitdirectory</code> in the sense that they exist as entities, but they are both partial implementations.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/danielhjacobs/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/danielhjacobs\">@danielhjacobs</a> Can you please confirm this.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I have updated the features appropriately.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3166057685\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40024\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/40024/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40024\">mdn/content#40024</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27178",
            "title": "FF141 File.webkitRelativePath / HTMLInputElement.webkitdirectory",
            "date_modified": "2025-06-30T01:20:26.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-06-30T01:19:33.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5179191?u=8dd92441fba3cb438759ee98862670ba56f2c67d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This PR changes all of the statements for Edge ≤79 to mirror from Chrome.  Based upon commit history and the data, it seems that most likely this data was all mirrored from Chrome via the original mirroring script anyways.</p>",
